2. **Environment validity and H-row handling are not explicitly preserved.** The smoke requires only “a verification verdict,” while the INVALID rule lists thinking failure and kernel-path differences ([009.md:41](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/plans/009.md:41), [009.md:72](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/plans/009.md:72)). Neither states what happens to H rows. Plan 007 specifies H-row handling, forbids rerunning agent failures, and has an environment-invalidity guard ([007.md:127](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/plans/007.md:127), [007.md:151](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/plans/007.md:151)). Its later ruling explicitly preserves the original rule for subsequent nonempty H rows ([007.md:232](/home/ubuntu/work/gemma/eval/plans/007.md:232)). Merely naming the same classifiers does not resolve this omission. Explicitly inherit the applicable smoke, validity, and rerun rules before allowing ON-ADOPT; do not generalize arm 1’s narrow empty-patch exemption.

